{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793381804,"nonce":"UD4kPihxY/TXygHylBiVoyf2JdU=","title":"Hybrid mode intermittently returns wrong results in PuffPuff's Canvas2D stroke tessellation","message":"Reported by the PuffPuff session. Ash 0.1.12, macOS arm64, machine load average 35-40.\n\n**What happens**\n\nIn hybrid (the default), a Canvas2D that should produce 300 draws produces 225: the 75 stroked open cubics (every 4th shape, width 2) yield zero vertices, so Canvas2D.draw returns early. Fills are right. The CPU mesh hash differs, so it is not GPU or upload. Once a process goes bad it stays bad. The first Canvas2D in the process (gpu.frame.vectors.submit) is correct; a later one with identical inputs (gpu.frame.vectors.readback) is wrong, which fits a tier promotion in between.\n\n--mode interp, --mode jit --jit-tier cranelift and --mode jit --jit-tier llvm were correct 6 of 6 runs each. Hybrid: 7 of 8 runs bad on the filter below; the full suite about 60%. Smaller filters do not reproduce.\n\n**Reproducer** (PuffPuff repo, ~/Vibranium/PuffPuff)\n\n    haxe build.hxml -cp tools/bench -main Suite -hl tools/snapshot/bin/Suite.hl\n    cd tools/snapshot/bin\n    ash Suite.hl time /tmp/out.json math,simd,canvas2d,quadbatcher,mesh,gpu.frame.vectors\n\nBad runs print \"FAIL: only 225 of 300 shapes produced vertices\". Candidates: Tessellate.hx (stroke), Flatten.hx, Sweep.hx, Canvas2D.hx; plain Haxe on Float and hl.Bytes.\n\n**Not yet tried**\n\n--jit-tier off, --no-tree-fusion, ASH_AIR=v2-serialize, ASH_NO_PROMOTE; narrowing to a function.","files":null}]}